title: "Input Group"
description: "A bordered field that joins an input or textarea with icons, text, and buttons on any side."
---

<script lang="ts">
	import Demo from "./demo.svelte";
</script>

# Input Group

Adds icons, text, or buttons inside the border of an input or textarea. Compose it from `InputGroup`, `InputGroupInput` or `InputGroupTextarea`, `InputGroupAddon`, `InputGroupButton`, and `InputGroupText`.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { InputGroup, InputGroupInput, InputGroupAddon } from "#lib/components/ui/input-group/index.js";
	import { SearchIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<InputGroup>
	<InputGroupInput placeholder="Search..." />
	<InputGroupAddon><SearchIcon /></InputGroupAddon>
	<InputGroupAddon align="inline-end">12 results</InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/input-group.json
```

## Anatomy

`InputGroup` draws the border, the focus ring, and the invalid ring around everything inside it. `InputGroupInput` and `InputGroupTextarea` are borderless controls that fill the group and accept the native attributes and `bind:value`. Each `InputGroupAddon` holds icons, text, or buttons, and clicking it outside a button focuses the control.

## Align

Set `align` on `InputGroupAddon` to `inline-start`, the default, or `inline-end` to place it beside the control, or to `block-start` or `block-end` to place it above or below. The markup order does not matter, so the control can come first for screen readers.

## Text

Wrap text, such as a prefix, suffix, or unit, in `InputGroupText` to mute it.

<Demo section="text" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroup>
	<InputGroupAddon><InputGroupText>https://</InputGroupText></InputGroupAddon>
	<InputGroupInput placeholder="example" />
	<InputGroupAddon align="inline-end"><InputGroupText>.com</InputGroupText></InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
```

## Button

`InputGroupButton` renders a compact ghost `Button` with `type="button"`, so it never submits a form unless you set `type="submit"`. It accepts every `Button` prop, such as `size="icon-xs"` for an icon. Give icon buttons an `aria-label`.

<Demo section="button" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroup>
	<InputGroupInput value="https://plainsv.com/r/input-group.json" readonly />
	<InputGroupAddon align="inline-end">
		<InputGroupButton size="icon-xs" aria-label="Copy" onclick={copyUrl}><CopyIcon /></InputGroupButton>
	</InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
```

## Textarea

Use `InputGroupTextarea` for multi-line text. It grows with its content. An addon with `align="block-end"` turns into a toolbar below it.

<Demo section="textarea" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroup>
	<InputGroupTextarea placeholder="Ask, search, or chat..." />
	<InputGroupAddon align="block-end">
		<InputGroupButton variant="outline" size="icon-xs" rounded="pill" aria-label="Add file"><PlusIcon /></InputGroupButton>
		<InputGroupButton variant="default" size="icon-xs" rounded="pill" aria-label="Send"><ArrowUpIcon /></InputGroupButton>
	</InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
```

## Sizes

Set `size` on `InputGroup` to `xs`, `sm`, `md`, or `lg`. The default is `md`, the height matches the input of the same size, and the padding, text size, and corner radius follow the size.

<Demo section="sizes" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroup size="sm">...</InputGroup>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` on `InputGroup` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the radius that follows `size`. Use `pill` for a one-line group. A group with a textarea or a `block-start` or `block-end` addon would become an oval as a pill, so use `3xl` or `4xl` for it.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroup rounded="pill">
	<InputGroupInput placeholder="Rounded pill" />
	<InputGroupAddon><SearchIcon /></InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
<InputGroup rounded="3xl">
	<InputGroupTextarea placeholder="Rounded 3xl with a textarea" />
	<InputGroupAddon align="block-end">
		<InputGroupButton variant="default" size="icon-xs" rounded="pill" aria-label="Send"><ArrowUpIcon /></InputGroupButton>
	</InputGroupAddon>
</InputGroup>
```

## States

Set `disabled` or `aria-invalid="true"` on the control, and the group dims or shows the invalid ring.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<InputGroupInput placeholder="Disabled" disabled />
<InputGroupInput placeholder="Invalid" aria-invalid="true" />
```

## API

`InputGroup` and `InputGroupAddon` extend the native `div` attributes. `InputGroupInput` and `InputGroupTextarea` extend the `input` and `textarea` attributes, and `InputGroupText` extends the `span` attributes. `InputGroupButton` takes the `Button` props.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Height, padding, and text size on the shared scale; defaults to `md` */
	size?: UiSize;
	/** Corner radius; follows `size` when omitted. `pill` is a true pill, so use `3xl` or `4xl` when the group stacks or holds a textarea */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}

interface AddonProps extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** `inline-start` and `inline-end` sit beside the input; `block-start` and `block-end` sit above and below it; defaults to `inline-start` */
	align?: "inline-start" | "inline-end" | "block-start" | "block-end";
}
```
